{"name":"Tranquil Aqua","hex":"#7c9aa0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tranquil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Free from emotional or mental disturbance.","Calm; without motion or sound."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tranquil"},{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tranquillity","blocks":[{"text":"Tranquillity is the quality or state of being tranquil; that is, calm, serene, and worry-free. The word tranquillity appears in numerous texts ranging from the religious writings of Buddhism—where the term passaddhi refers to tranquillity of the body, thoughts, and consciousness on the path to enlightenment—to an assortment of policy and planning guidance documents, where interpretation of the word is typically linked to engagement with the natural environment. It is also famously used in the Preamble to the United States Constitution, which describes one of the purposes for which the document was establishing the government as to \"insure domestic Tranquility\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/John-constable-the-hay-wain.jpg/330px-John-constable-the-hay-wain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tranquillity"},{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg/500px-Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg/1280px-Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg/500px-Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Nature_Ambience_Badagry%2C_Lagos_Nigeria_May_2023.jpg/500px-Nature_Ambience_Badagry%2C_Lagos_Nigeria_May_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Nature_Ambience_Badagry%2C_Lagos_Nigeria_May_2023.jpg/1280px-Nature_Ambience_Badagry%2C_Lagos_Nigeria_May_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Nature_Ambience_Badagry%2C_Lagos_Nigeria_May_2023.jpg/500px-Nature_Ambience_Badagry%2C_Lagos_Nigeria_May_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Serenity Bagagry, Lagos Nigeria. ","link":"https://en.wiki